  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word used primarily in political, historical, and legal contexts. Implies legitimate or de facto political authority over a territory or people.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {支配|しはい}: domination, control (can imply oppressive rule)\n- {治世|ちせい}: reign, rule (focuses on the period of rule)\n- {政治|せいじ}: politics, government (broader, refers to the system)\n- {統制|とうせい}: control, regulation (focuses on managing/regulating)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {統治|とうち}{権|けん}: governing authority, sovereignty\n- {統治|とうち}{者|しゃ}: ruler, governor\n- {統治|とうち}{体制|たいせい}: system of governance\n- {植民地|しょくみんち}{統治|とうち}: colonial rule\n- {統治|とうち}{機構|きこう}: governing structure",
